\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Commutant matrices in declared bases}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Choose a right #{D_\Xi}-basis of the
[multiplicity module](fdip-00KN) and realize each basis element by an
isometric copy of #{W_\Xi}. In that basis an element of the commutant
is a matrix #{A\in M_{m_\Xi}(D_\Xi)} acting by
#{(Aw)_i=\sum_jA_{ij}(w_j)}. The adjoint of \ref{fdip-004Z} becomes
conjugate transpose. The scalar-side warning remains: #{D_\Xi} acts
on #{W_\Xi} on the left, and quaternion products are not reversed.}

\p{For a vertex permutation representation, the vertex indicator basis
makes the same commutant the span of the orbital indicator matrices.
An entry #{A_{u,v}} depends only on the orbit of #{(u,v)}.}
